# Copy this file to .env (in the repo root, next to this file) and fill in
# the values below. Never commit your actual .env -- it's gitignored on
# purpose.
#
# One file for both setups:
# - `pnpm run dev`: the server loads it with `bun --env-file=../.env`
#   (server/package.json), and the Prisma CLI through prisma7.config.ts.
# - `docker compose up`: passed to the container by compose.yaml. Only
#   OPENAI_API_KEY and MAX_UPLOAD_MB apply there; the paths and port below
#   are fixed inside the container.

# Required for `pnpm run dev`. Used server-side only (transcription via
# Whisper and the AI buttons) -- never exposed to the browser. Optional
# with Docker, where the app asks for it on first launch instead.
OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...

# Optional. Largest accepted video upload, in MB (default 10240 = 10GB).
# Uploads stream straight to disk, so this is about disk space, not memory.
# MAX_UPLOAD_MB=10240

# --- Development only (the defaults below are what's used if unset) ---

# Resolved relative to server/, where the backend runs from.
# DATABASE_URL="file:./data/app.db"

# Root directory for all local project data (uploads, transcripts, renders).
# DATA_DIR="./data"

# Port the Hono/Bun server listens on. The Vite client's dev server proxies
# /api/* requests here (see client/vite.config.mts).
# PORT=3001

# Origin allowed to make cross-origin requests in dev (the Vite dev server).
# CORS_ORIGIN="http://localhost:5173"

# Overrides the `ffmpeg` binary used for rendering. Only needed if your
# default `ffmpeg` lacks libass (subtitle burn-in support) -- on Homebrew,
# `brew install ffmpeg-full` gets you one that has it, and this points at
# it instead of the default `ffmpeg` on PATH. Without this, "Burn in
# captions" will fail with "No such filter: 'subtitles'" if your default
# ffmpeg build doesn't include libass. FFPROBE_PATH does the same for
# ffprobe.
# FFMPEG_PATH="/opt/homebrew/opt/ffmpeg-full/bin/ffmpeg"
